#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ghtk -- streamlined GitHub CLI (pull requests, issues, reviews, CI) for skills and humans.

A single self-contained, stdlib-only tool. See README.md for the usage contract.
Run `ghtk`, `ghtk <group> --help`, or `ghtk <group> <command> --help` for help.

Design notes for maintainers:
  - HTTP is plain `urllib.request` (no `gh`, no `requests`). This is deliberate: the `gh`
    CLI is a Go binary whose macOS system-trust TLS verification FAILS inside the Seatbelt
    sandbox (x509: OSStatus -26276), which is why the old per-skill scripts had to run with
    the sandbox disabled. urllib honors HTTP(S)_PROXY via getproxies() and uses OpenSSL's
    file-based verifier, so with a real CA bundle it reaches api.github.com *inside* the
    sandbox -- no bypass needed.
  - TLS: some Python builds (python.org macOS framework builds) ship an EMPTY CA trust store,
    so HTTPS fails with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED regardless of any sandbox. build_ssl_context()
    resolves a CA bundle at runtime (env -> Python store -> certifi -> cached -> macOS keychain
    export -> known Linux bundles) so it works on macOS and Linux, even where ~/.config is
    read-only. Ported from the atlassian-toolkit.
  - Auth: a GitHub token via Authorization: Bearer. Precedence: GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN env ->
    `gh auth token` (reuses an existing gh login, keychain read works in-sandbox) ->
    ~/.config/github-toolkit/auth.json. `ghtk auth login` is the fallback for machines without gh.
  - REST at api.github.com (Accept: application/vnd.github+json); GraphQL at /graphql. GraphQL
    returns errors INSIDE HTTP 200, so graphql() checks the errors[] array before unwrapping data.
  - Output favors compact text to keep token cost low; --json is the structured escape hatch.
  - Writes (pr comment/reply/resolve/create) all support --dry-run: they print the exact request
    (method, URL, JSON body) and send nothing, so the whole surface is exercisable read-only.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fnmatch
